  "status": "published",
  "title": "Steel Pipe Bookshelf",
  "summary": "Three 32 in stained pine shelves held apart by 3/4 in black iron pipe and floor flanges. Industrial look, screwed together, no welding.",
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "estimatedHours": 6,
  "imageUrl": null,
  "currency": "USD",
  "steps": [
    "Wipe every pipe and flange with mineral spirits and a rag until the rag stays clean; the factory oil will otherwise rub off on books and hands.",
    "Spray the pipe parts with two light coats of clear lacquer to keep them from rusting.",
    "Cut the 2x10 into three 32 in shelves, sand them from 80 to 220 grit, and apply one coat of stain followed by two coats of polyurethane.",
    "Mark a flange position 1 1/2 in in from each corner on both faces of the middle shelf, the underside of the top shelf and both faces of the bottom shelf, and screw the flanges on.",
    "Thread the 4 in nipples into the bottom shelf's underside flanges with a foot flange on each, then thread the 12 in nipples between the shelves, turning each column a little at a time to keep the shelves level.",
    "Stand the unit against the wall, check it is level, and screw the anti-tip strap into a wall stud."
  ],
